1
00:00:04,010 --> 00:00:05,865
Hi, I'm Chris.

2
00:00:05,865 --> 00:00:07,845
I'm a Diversity Program
Manager here at Google.

3
00:00:07,845 --> 00:00:10,410
Influencing is a huge component

4
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:12,345
when it comes to
program management.

5
00:00:12,345 --> 00:00:16,335
You might have an incredible idea

6
00:00:16,335 --> 00:00:19,920
about where you want a
program or a project to go,

7
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:21,420
and so once you have

8
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:23,310
come up with all
these creative ideas,

9
00:00:23,310 --> 00:00:26,325
and you want to convince
someone to sign off on it,

10
00:00:26,325 --> 00:00:28,830
you have to think about
what's in it for them.

11
00:00:28,830 --> 00:00:30,750
What's the impact
that this project or

12
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:33,090
program is going to
have on the business,

13
00:00:33,090 --> 00:00:35,130
on the consumer, what have you,

14
00:00:35,130 --> 00:00:37,290
and so once you are
able to distill

15
00:00:37,290 --> 00:00:40,125
what that impact is going to be,

16
00:00:40,125 --> 00:00:43,460
you can really think
about how you're going to

17
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:47,995
frame the ask to that
executive stakeholder.

18
00:00:47,995 --> 00:00:51,485
Influencing, everyone has
the ability to do it.

19
00:00:51,485 --> 00:00:52,760
You've done it since
you were a kid,

20
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:54,110
whether it be trying
to go out and

21
00:00:54,110 --> 00:00:55,610
play with your friends or get

22
00:00:55,610 --> 00:00:56,885
your favorite meal from

23
00:00:56,885 --> 00:00:58,490
the favorite restaurant
that you have.

24
00:00:58,490 --> 00:00:59,960
You've always tried to influence

25
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:01,520
someone to give
you what you want,

26
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:04,205
but you have to think about
what the value is for them.

27
00:01:04,205 --> 00:01:06,095
So different, when you're a kid,

28
00:01:06,095 --> 00:01:07,565
the value is only really for you.

29
00:01:07,565 --> 00:01:09,230
When I first came into my role

30
00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:10,910
as a diversity program manager,

31
00:01:10,910 --> 00:01:13,370
there were a set of programs

32
00:01:13,370 --> 00:01:16,325
that had been around
for a number of years,

33
00:01:16,325 --> 00:01:17,900
and I came in,

34
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:18,950
I had a fresh set of eyes,

35
00:01:18,950 --> 00:01:20,840
and I recognized that
there's a lot of

36
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:23,275
redundancy with the
programs that we had.

37
00:01:23,275 --> 00:01:25,550
What I did is came in and I

38
00:01:25,550 --> 00:01:26,720
had to influence people that

39
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:28,130
had been running those programs,

40
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:30,290
that their programs were

41
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:32,870
all very similar in that
if we all work together,

42
00:01:32,870 --> 00:01:34,460
we'd be able to build

43
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:37,795
just one program that
solves all these needs.

44
00:01:37,795 --> 00:01:39,630
Now that took some time, right?

45
00:01:39,630 --> 00:01:42,320
I had to show examples
of why I think

46
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:46,580
this singular
program could impact

47
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:50,825
the target population in the
same way I had to show how

48
00:01:50,825 --> 00:01:55,430
each person would have a role
in this new found program, right?

49
00:01:55,430 --> 00:01:57,380
I couldn't just say like all

50
00:01:57,380 --> 00:01:59,335
of your programs need to stop.

51
00:01:59,335 --> 00:02:01,850
It was more so all your
programs need to mature

52
00:02:01,850 --> 00:02:05,420
into this new identity,

53
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:07,100
so it took some time.

54
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:09,650
It really also took a lot of

55
00:02:09,650 --> 00:02:13,205
relationship massaging
and maturing

56
00:02:13,205 --> 00:02:14,480
because I was a new guy,

57
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:16,090
so I had to come in
and prove myself.

58
00:02:16,090 --> 00:02:18,335
The impact was shown

59
00:02:18,335 --> 00:02:20,600
pretty soon after because

60
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:22,555
it was thought through
well in advance.

61
00:02:22,555 --> 00:02:26,235
My advice is: keep it simple.

62
00:02:26,235 --> 00:02:28,520
So, you have all of

63
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:32,165
the background information
about why this is important,

64
00:02:32,165 --> 00:02:34,790
all the steps it will
take you to get there,

65
00:02:34,790 --> 00:02:36,590
but the person who you're

66
00:02:36,590 --> 00:02:38,240
trying to influence just needs to

67
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:40,220
know when you're going to get

68
00:02:40,220 --> 00:02:42,260
there and basic information

69
00:02:42,260 --> 00:02:43,520
on how you're going to get there.

70
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:45,990
And so, don't try to bring
them into the weeds with you.

71
00:02:45,990 --> 00:02:47,615
Keep them at a point

72
00:02:47,615 --> 00:02:50,020
that makes sense for the
audience that you're in.

73
00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:51,590
So if you're talking
to a researcher,

74
00:02:51,590 --> 00:02:53,510
they might want to
know the data points.

75
00:02:53,510 --> 00:02:55,830
So, talking to the marketing team,

76
00:02:55,830 --> 00:02:57,225
they want to probably know

77
00:02:57,225 --> 00:02:59,690
the more splashy
high-level elements

78
00:02:59,690 --> 00:03:00,980
and the target demographics.

79
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:03,170
So keep in mind your
audience, but keep it simple.

80
00:03:03,170 --> 00:03:05,630
Influencing doesn't
need to be a chore.

81
00:03:05,630 --> 00:03:07,010
Once you've done the work,

82
00:03:07,010 --> 00:03:09,140
you should be excited to
talk to someone about it,

83
00:03:09,140 --> 00:03:10,190
and so, if you don't feel

84
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:11,765
excited about the work
that you're doing,

85
00:03:11,765 --> 00:03:13,310
I would take a step
back and think

86
00:03:13,310 --> 00:03:15,920
about what it is that
you are building,

87
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:17,675
what it is that you're
putting together,

88
00:03:17,675 --> 00:03:20,730
and if it doesn't excite you,

89
00:03:20,730 --> 00:03:22,900
it's not going to
excite somebody else.
